{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
Group B was one of four groups of national teams competing in the second stage of the [[1982 FIFA World Cup]]. The group's three matches were staged at the [[Santiago Bernabéu Stadium|Santiago Bernabéu]] in [[Madrid]]. The group consisted of three teams advancing from the first group stage: Group 2 winners [[Germany national football team|West Germany]], Group 5 runners-up, the host nation [[Spain national football team|Spain]], and Group 4 winners [[England national football team|England]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/82full.html |title=World Cup 1982 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> England finished the group without scoring or conceding a single goal, the only time that has ever happened in any kind of group in FIFA World Cup history. Like [[Scotland national football team|Scotland]] in [[1974 FIFA World Cup|'74]] and [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]] in [[1978 FIFA World Cup|'78]], [[England national football team|''Three Lions'' of '82]] stayed unbeaten but were eliminated before the semi-finals. Their elimination was the result of only managing a goalless draw against already-eliminated Spain in the final group match, though even a win would not have kept England in the competition unless it was by at least two clear goals.

West Germany topped the group and advanced to the semi-finals.

==Qualified teams==
The winners of Group 2 and 4 and the runner-up of Group 5 qualified for Group B of the second round.

